INT. COURTHOUSE HOLDING CELL - DAY

Cinderblock. A bench. A caged lightbulb. ATTORNEY BERNADETTE FALCONER-ADU (40s, navy suit) leans on the bars. Her client, MARCELINO TORRIJOS (30s, orange jumpsuit), sits with his head in his hands. A deputy, LIAM OYELARAN-STACK (20s), stands guard.

The intercom crackles.

                    CLERK (V.O.)
          Case 4417, State versus Torrijos, five minutes.

She checks her watch. He lifts his head. She nods once.

He stands and offers her a sealed envelope. She hesitates, then takes it.

The deputy steps forward. She shows him the envelope. He glances inside, nods, and unlocks the door. She slips it into her briefcase. He returns to his post.

                    CLERK (V.O.)
          Counsel, please approach.

She squeezes Marcelino's shoulder. He stares at the floor.

The door buzzes open. She walks out. He watches her go. The deputy locks the door.

The intercom clicks off. The bulb flickers. Marcelino sits down, slowly, and waits.
